s of \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) onto the directrix are \\( A' \\) and \\( B' \\), respectively.\n    Since the directrix is \\( x = -p/2 \\),:\n   \n    \\[\n    A' = \\left( -\\frac{p}{2}, y_1 \\right) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad B' = \\left( -\\frac{p}{2}, y_2 \\right)\n    \\]\n   \n4. **Calculation of Areas:**\n\n    Determine the probability that a point \\( M \\) inside quadrilateral \\( AA'B'B \\) falls within \\( \\triangle F A'B' \\).\n   \n    1) **Area of \\( \\triangle F A'B' \\):**\n    \n    Since \\( F = \\left( \\frac{p}{2}, 0 \\right) \\), using the formula for the area of a triangle, we have:\n    \n    \\[\n    \\text{Area}(\\triangle FA'B') = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\frac{p}{2} - \\left( -\\frac{p}{2} \\right) \\right| \\cdot \\left| y_1 - y_2 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot p \\cdot \\left| y_1 - y_2 \\right|\n    \\]\n   \n    2) **Area of Quadrilateral \\( AA'B'B \\):**\n    \n    The area of the quadrilateral can be split into trapezoids:\n    \n    \\[\n    \\text{Area}(A A' B' B) = \\left| A'A \\right| \\cdot \\left| A'B' \\right| + \\left| B'B \\right| \\cdot \\left| A'B' \\right|\n    \\]\n    \n    As the height from \\( A \\) down to \\( l \\) (similarly for \\( B \\)) is \\( p \\):\n    \n    \\[\n    \\text{Area}(A A' B' B) = \\left( |AF| + |BF| \\right) \\cdot p = 3p \\cdot p\n    \\]\n   \n5. **Finding the Probability:**\n   \n    The probability that a point \\( M \\) inside the quadrilateral falls within \\( \\triangle F A'B' \\) is the ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the quadrilateral:\n    \n    \\[\n    \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Area}(\\triangle FA'B')}{\\text{Area}(AA'B'B)} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot p \\cdot \\left| y_1 - y_2 \\right|}{3p^2} = \\frac{\\left| y_1 - y_2 \\right|}{6p}\n    \\]\n    \n6. **Solving for Relative Lengths:**\n\n    From the given \\( |AB| = 3p \\), the harmonic mean or total span of the section \\( |AB| \\) and projections yields:\n    \n    \\[\n    \\frac{1}{3}\n    \\]\n\n### 